{"t": 1794105432.7085679, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "Incident update \u2014 PaymentGatewayErrors (checkout, AG-7731)\n\nWhat's wrong: since 07:41 UTC ~38% of gateway charge calls return 400 invalid_amount. Gateway API moved to 2026-11 \"strict amounts\" and now requires amount as an integer in minor units (cents). checkout/gateway.py was still sending a decimal EUR value (e.g. 12.34), so every charge was rejected. Customer-facing: charges are failing, not mis-charged.\n\nFix: checkout/gateway.py now converts EUR to integer cents (round half up via Decimal, so 1.15 -> 115, not 114) and keeps currency=EUR. Verified locally across edge cases (0.01, 1.15, 12.34, 1234.56). No other callers of charge_payload changed.\n\nNext: needs deploy to prod-eu-1; 4xx rate should drop once traffic hits the new build. Alert AG-7731 can be resolved after that. Nothing to do on the gateway side \u2014 the API change is intentional."}, "ok": true}
